RULED 2026-10-24 — the spelling is now legal-by-construction.

`| number u64[\d+]` parses today: a trailing `[…]` on a type position is a
compiler annotation (opaque string, comma list), extracted into
`type_annotations` on the payload's `__type_ref` field — same lane as
`Source[text]` in 210_039. The branch types here are legal Koru.

What remains aspirational is the FEATURE the annotations were written for —
a parser-generator transform that consumes them (`derive(parser)`, the
`~[…]` literate doc block with directives). Nothing reads `type_annotations`
on branch payloads yet; this test parks as the second witness of the
surface, not the feature. `main` is still empty — the declared `token`
event is never emitted.
